#
# omx-clap-core.abi — the thread roles of omx-clap-core's embedding API, declared once (omx-rt-gate(1)).
# `--abi omx-clap-core` binds the library side (omx-clap-core: its core and its LV2 adapter), and
# `--abi omx-clap-core:host` the embedder that hands the library these functions (plugin-hostd, any host
# of the adapter). There, each function stored into one of these fields is a root of the role named,
# judged in the embedder's own run.
#
# what the embedder provides: the library calls these from the audio thread
#   omx_clap_audio_role.is_audio   the audio-role predicate omx_clap_host_set_audio_role and
#                                  omx_clap_host_publish_role hand in: is this thread the instance's
#                                  audio thread (the CLAP host's thread check, a helper's task)
#   lv2_audio_role.is_audio        the same predicate for an LV2 instance (lv2_instance_set_role),
#                                  asked by schedule_work and the log on the audio thread
#   omx_lv2_feature_options.sink   the log sink a plugin's log:log line is routed to
#                                  (OMX_LV2_LOG_ROUTE), called with the formatted line from the
#                                  plugin's audio thread
host omx_clap_audio_role is_audio audio
host lv2_audio_role is_audio audio
host omx_lv2_feature_options sink audio
